# Lesson Publishing & Integrity

Companion to [`lesson-code-block-conventions.mdc`](./lesson-code-block-conventions.mdc) (which governs *how code blocks are labelled*) and [`methodology-page-structure.mdc`](./methodology-page-structure.mdc) (slug-directory layout).

**This file governs whether the page is actually correct once published.** Every rule below was written after a real defect shipped into this repo. None of them are hypothetical.

> The failure mode this file exists to prevent: **the build succeeds, the page loads, and the content is silently wrong.** Nothing warns you. A student finds it.

---

## 1. Liquid runs inside code fences — wrap or lose your code

Jekyll processes Liquid **everywhere in a `.md` file, including fenced code blocks.** Any `{{ … }}` or `{% … %}` is evaluated and, if it isn't valid Liquid, **silently deleted from the published HTML**.

Real breakage found in this repo:

| Source | Published as |
| --- | --- |
| `<Navigate ... replace state={{ from: location }} />` | `<Navigate ... replace state= />` |
| `--shard=${{ matrix.shard }}/3` | `--shard=$/3` |
| `${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}` | *(empty)* |
| `style={{ marginLeft: 8 }}` | *(attribute gutted)* |

**Rule:** any code fence containing `{{`, `}}`, `{%`, or `${{` **must** be wrapped:

~~~~markdown
{% raw %}

```jsx
<Navigate to={redirectTo} replace state={{ from: location }} />
```

{% endraw %}
~~~~

Applies to **JSX object literals/style props, GitHub Actions expressions, Vue/Angular/Handlebars templates, and Liquid being taught as a subject.**

**Enforcement:** `.github/workflows/pages.yml` fails the build on `Liquid Warning`. Never silence it — fix the fence. Check locally before committing:

```bash
cd web-foundations && npm run build 2>&1 | grep "Liquid Warning"
```

---

## 1b. Liquid includes must emit flush-left HTML

Kramdown treats **indented** HTML as a fenced code block. After Liquid expands an `{% include %}`, any line that begins with a tab or four spaces can publish as escaped markup (`&lt;nav…&gt;`) instead of a live element — the lang switcher looked like raw source on the page.

**Rule:** includes that emit block HTML (`<nav>`, `<figure>`, `<div>`, …) must output **every line at column 0**. No tab-indented children. Prefer a single compact line in the include file. When `_config.yml` sets `parse_block_html: true`, add **`markdown="0"`** on the outermost wrapper so Kramdown does not re-parse inner tags as Markdown (symptom: `&lt;/nav&gt;&lt;/div&gt;` visible on the page and the rest of the lesson nested inside an unclosed element).

**Verify after building:**

```bash
grep -A2 'track-lang-switch' web-foundations/docs/_site/tracks/fei/index.html
# Must show <nav class="track-lang-switch"> — not <pre><code>&lt;nav
```

Applies to track lang switchers, curriculum figures inlined via include, and any future `_includes/*.html` dropped into Markdown lessons.

