## 6. Cite only what you verified

An FE II unit shipped **five fabricated "Key Findings"** attributed to a real paper (Oliveira et al. 2026). In a course whose central assessment artefact is an AI Use Declaration, that is disqualifying.

**Rule:**

- Only cite a source you have **actually read or that is recorded in [`profield-frontend-pedagogy.md`](../../frontend-pedagogy/profield-frontend-pedagogy.md)** with its identifier and findings.
- Reproduce the **real numbers**, including unflattering ones (~32–33% responsiveness is the honest figure; teach it).
- Carry the **scope caveat** into the lesson. If the evidence is from a different cohort, say so — an `[UNVERIFIED-GAP]` is a legitimate teaching point ("you are inside the gap"), not something to paper over.
- `[UNVERIFIED-NOISE]` claims are excluded from lesson design entirely.
- **Never invent a URL** — sandbox links, DOIs, endpoints. If it must exist and you cannot create it, mark it clearly and escalate to the professor.

### 6.1 Publish the citation, keep the machinery in source

Student pages use Chicago author-date by default: `(Author Year, page)`. A
direct quotation requires a page. Every lesson with research citations ends
with `## References` or `## Referencias`, containing complete Chicago entries.

Do not publish local research architecture: Ahmes/Athanor/DevIAC names,
`[BIBLIO-GAP]`, `evaluator_safe`, coat/node IDs, extraction database/schema
names, project keys, vector-search notes, or local paths. Preserve all of it in
the lesson Markdown beside the relevant claim, but behind the fail-closed
switch:

```liquid
{% if site.publication.publish_internal_metadata %}
<!-- curriculum-internal:
[BIBLIO-GAP or VERIFIED]
Ahmes anchor: <db>; node: <id>; page: <n>; evaluator_safe=<yes|no>
discovery/transfer notes: <complete audit trail>
-->
{% endif %}
```

`publication.publish_internal_metadata` defaults to `false`; absence also
means false. Enabling it is an explicit private-debug operation. The normal
build must fail if any forbidden metadata reaches rendered HTML or assets.
An unresolved source never receives a polished author-date citation: retain
the audit privately, and either omit the claim or teach it as an open question
without the internal status label.

