## 7. Quotes come from TTOD, with their ID

Epigraphs are not decoration and must not be improvised. Source them from `/Users/ruvebal/src/ttod/ttod.yml` (213 quotes) and cite the ID so they stay traceable:

```markdown
> _"Code without quality checks is like a ship without a compass: it moves, but who knows where."_
> — Tao of Development, `qa-009`
```

Sections: `images`, `architecture`, `code-craft`, `qa-tooling`, `wisdom`, `remote-repo`, `devops`, `debugging`, `ux`, `accessibility`, `javascript`. Place them at conceptual turns — the opening frame, each major pivot, the close — not every heading.

> ⚠️ `web-foundations/docs/_data/ttod.yml` is a **stale copy** (176 quotes vs 213 upstream). Quote statically in Markdown; don't rely on `site.data.ttod` for newer IDs until it's re-synced.

**The site tagline is exactly "Critical Coding for a Better Living" — never extend it.** It is pre-existing site identity (homepage, footer, `methodology/en/index.md`). An earlier pass appended *"…for all humans and machines"* on the track pages and in a unit; Rubén reverted it (2026-08-10). Quote the tagline verbatim or not at all — and never write prose that quotes a *half* of it (`The "for machines" half of our vision…`), since that breaks the moment the wording is corrected. Express the idea in your own words instead.

